WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
Welcome to our training on how to upload your own size charts for your products in Seller Central.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.907
Our self-service size chart tool can help you upload a new size chart or edit an existing one without

00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:15.440
contacting Selling Partner Support.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.320
Size charts are the industry standard for sizing communication.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:25.073
Customers rely on size charts to understand product sizing and make informed purchase decisions

00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:28.360
on the best fit for their body measurements.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:35.022
Including accurate and reliable sizing information helps reduce customer returns due to incorrect

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:36.560
sizing or fit.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.850
In this training, we will review what information to include in your size charts, how to upload

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:49.880
them, how to edit existing size charts, and how to bulk upload up to 1,000 ASINs at a time.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.360
To get started, you'll need to know what information needs to be included in your size chart.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.693
This can vary depending on your product, as well as if you are including only local or local and

00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:02.360
international sizes.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.760
To create your size chart, you will need three pieces of information.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.760
First, your brand size.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.993
These are the sizes listed on your manufacturer label and should be the exact sizes the customer

00:01:14.993 --> 00:01:19.760
references when choosing from the size selector drop-down on your product page.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.960
Second, you will need the corresponding body measurements.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.760
These will vary based on the product.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:32.124
For example, men's pants will typically require waist and in-seam measurements, whereas women's

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:35.760
dresses may require bust, waist, and hip measurements.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.760
You will need these measurements for each brand size you sell.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.760
These can be a range or one value and should be in the local unit of measurement.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.760
Third, you may need to include other country sizes as well as local sizes in your size chart.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:57.348
This is especially important for products like shoes which don't always have universal translations

00:01:57.348 --> 00:01:58.760
between international sizes.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:04.655
Once you have all the essential information for your product, you can get started with uploading

00:02:04.655 --> 00:02:05.760
your size chart.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.305
To access our self-service size chart tool, go to Catalog in the Seller Central main menu, then

00:02:12.305 --> 00:02:13.760
click Add Size Charts.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:20.189
The size chart tool is available for brand representatives and authorized resellers who have been

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:22.760
registered through the Amazon brand registry.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:30.653
You gain automatic entry to the tool upon registration if you have a product listing in apparel,

00:02:30.653 --> 00:02:35.760
shoes, sports, or outdoors where body size chart information is applicable.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.792
If you're unable to access the size chart tool, you can contact your primary account manager to

00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:46.760
enable size chart permissions by clicking the Settings icon and going to User Permissions.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:52.760
To edit or upload a new size chart, first, select your target location.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.760
Next, search for an ASIN.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:03:01.427
Once you have selected your location and ASIN, you will be able to download a size chart template

00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:04.760
based on the location and product type you selected.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:11.737
To add or edit a size chart for multiple ASINs under one product type, you can search for any ASIN

00:03:11.737 --> 00:03:17.318
within that product type that is currently using the correct size chart and it will automatically

00:03:17.318 --> 00:03:19.760
load the parent ASIN in the tool.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.760
Depending on the product, you may have the option to choose between a pre-filled template with existing

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.760
measurements based on the ASIN or a blank template.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:35.760
If there isn't a size chart template available for the ASIN you selected, check that your website

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.525
display group, department attribute, and product type don't have any catalog defects before contacting

00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:42.760
Selling Partner Support.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:49.510
If the size chart still is not available, you can contact Selling Partner Support to submit a request

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.760
for a new size chart template.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.918
Size chart templates are location specific and measurements and information requirements will be

00:03:57.918 --> 00:04:00.760
unique to the location you selected.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.760
Templates are downloaded as Excel files.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:09.760
Make sure you don't add or delete rows or columns as this will cause your template upload to fail.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:16.392
Now you're ready to enter or edit the measurements in your template based on your ASIN or product

00:04:16.392 --> 00:04:16.760
type.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:22.189
Any cells you leave empty will not appear on the size chart when it is published on the product

00:04:22.189 --> 00:04:22.760
detail page.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:29.617
Make sure to submit all measurements in the same unit, such as centimeters or inches, that is listed

00:04:29.617 --> 00:04:30.760
in the template.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:36.942
If necessary, the unit type will be automatically converted for you when the size chart is published

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.760
on the product detail page.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:44.991
After you have added all the measurements for your ASIN or product type, you will select from one

00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:47.760
of two ways to apply your size chart.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.760
The first option you can select is across product type.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:57.960
This will apply your size chart to all ASINs across one product type from your brand, for example,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.760
Men's Pants.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.093
This is the least recommended option since different ASINs in a product group could have different

00:05:04.093 --> 00:05:07.760
sizing schemes or measurements that are specific to a certain ASINs.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:15.760
ASINs with an existing single chart upload will be excluded from product type uploads.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.760
The second option you can choose is Select ASINs.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:26.093
This allows you to apply your size chart to a single ASIN or multiple ASINs under one location and

00:05:26.093 --> 00:05:26.760
product type.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:33.189
Whenever possible, try to upload only one size chart table to a single ASIN to ensure the information

00:05:33.189 --> 00:05:36.760
is as accurate and specific to the ASIN as possible.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:43.760
Choosing this option is most likely to reduce returns related to incorrect sizing and fit.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:50.803
However, you can upload up to three size chart tables when uploading to a single ASIN to support

00:05:50.803 --> 00:05:52.760
ASINs with specific sizing information.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:59.760
For example, a set that includes top and bottom measurements or a plus and regular size chart.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.760
You can add up to 1,000 unique ASINs when using the Select ASIN option.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.760
Once you have added your ASINs, click Validate.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:13.760
A notification will pop up to let you know if they were validated successfully.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:20.348
If any were not validated, click Download the Validation Report in the notification box to learn

00:06:20.348 --> 00:06:20.760
why.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:25.760
You can still proceed with the size chart upload for all validated ASINs.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:31.578
Once your ASINs have been validated, you can upload your completed size chart template into the

00:06:31.578 --> 00:06:33.760
Self Service Size Chart Upload tool.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.760
If your template was filled out correctly, you will see a preview of your size chart.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:43.760
Review the size chart preview carefully to ensure everything is correct.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:50.240
If your size chart has errors, you may get a notification to correct these errors and re-upload

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.760
your size chart before you can publish.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:59.076
Errors may include mismatched sizes from your size selector on the product page, missing measurements,

00:06:59.076 --> 00:07:00.760
incorrect units of measurement,

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:06.760
incorrect measurement range order, or garment measurements being used instead of body measurements.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:13.060
Correct the errors listed in your error report in the Excel template, and then re-upload the template

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:13.760
to continue.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:18.760
The size chart preview will populate when all errors have been addressed.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:24.760
After double-checking your size chart preview, your size chart is ready to publish.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:31.412
Size charts will be visible on your Amazon product detail page within 8 hours of publishing through

00:07:31.412 --> 00:07:33.760
our Self Service Size Chart tool.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:39.710
Now you're ready to start uploading and editing your own size charts with our Self Service Size

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:40.760
Chart Upload tool.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.760
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
